## 🛠️ What Changed & Added

### 1. Backend In-Memory Room Management & WebRTC Signaling
- **File**: [`server.py`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main/server.py)
  - Created `RoomManager` class supporting rooms capped at 2 participants for the MVP.
  - Implemented `/ws/meeting/{room_id}/{peer_id}` signaling WebSocket handling:
    - `join`: Registers peer and responds with `room_joined` containing existing peer details and initiator status.
    - `offer` & `answer`: Relays standard WebRTC Session Description Protocol (SDP) packets directly between peers.
    - `ice_candidate`: Relays ICE candidate packets for peer-to-peer NAT traversal.
    - `track_state`: Synchronizes camera and microphone enabled/disabled states.
    - `leave` & disconnect handling: Broadcasts `participant_left` to the remaining peer so the UI cleans up immediately.
  - Bound Uvicorn to `0.0.0.0:8000` for seamless local network / Wi-Fi testing.

### 2. Frontend WebRTC Modular Integration
- **File**: [`frontend/src/utils/webrtc.js`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/frontend/src/utils/webrtc.js)
  - Modularized `RTCPeerConnection` configuration with Google STUN (`stun:stun.l.google.com:19302`).
  - Track addition and stream lifecycle management.
- **File**: [`frontend/src/components/JoinModal.jsx`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/frontend/src/components/JoinModal.jsx)
  - Polished room join modal prompting for **Display Name** (e.g. Sarthak / Rahul) and **Room ID** (e.g. CODE26) adhering to SilentMeet's glassmorphism style.
- **File**: [`frontend/src/components/VideoStage.jsx`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/frontend/src/components/VideoStage.jsx)
  - Replaced static avatar placeholders with real `<video>` and `<audio>` elements for connected remote peers.
  - Shows dynamic camera-off avatars and muted indicators.
  - Shows a "Waiting for Participant" state with the room code when only 1 user is present.
- **File**: [`frontend/src/components/Header.jsx`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/frontend/src/components/Header.jsx)
  - Dynamic room code badge with click-to-copy functionality.
  - Real-time WebRTC connection pill (`🟢 Connected`, `🟡 Connecting P2P...`, `Waiting for Peer`).
- **File**: [`frontend/src/App.jsx`](file:///d:/project/hand-gesture-recognition-using-mediapipe-main%20-%20Copy%20-%20Copy/frontend/src/App.jsx)
  - Dynamic host calculation (`window.location.hostname`) ensuring cross-device LAN compatibility.
  - Dual-channel WebSocket architecture: `/ws/meeting/...` for WebRTC signaling and `/ws/gestures` for MediaPipe AI messages.
  - Continuous MediaPipe AI vision loop (~7 FPS) seamlessly operating on the local webcam stream without hardware locks or conflicts.

